<p>{% person "frank-l-nigey" %}Frank L. Nigey{% endperson %} built a three-story brick hotel in 1906 for the luxury market, then served only by the {% place "inter-ocean-hotel" %}InterOcean Hotel{% endplace %} one block closer to the {% place "northern-pacific-first-passenger-depot" %}Northern Pacific depot{% endplace %}. The Nigey Hotel had electric service, hot and cold running water in every room, shared bathrooms on each floor, and local and long-distance telephone service.</p>

