<p>The original building had front and rear rows of rooms parallel to Third Avenue Northwest. Its success led to an addition that more than doubled the hotel's size. Beginning in June 1917, the expanded building housed the city's first telephone exchange near its First Avenue Northwest entrance and in the basement. {% place "dahners-music-and-department-store" %}Dahners Music Store{% endplace %} also occupied the building. From 1920 to 1928, {% person "d-c-mohr" %}D. C. Mohr{% endperson %} operated Mandan's first {% place "j-c-penney" %}J. C. Penney{% endplace %} store there.</p>

