<p>In 1910, nightly rates at Mandan hotels ranged from $1 at the {% place "peoples-hotel" %}Hotel Mandan{% endplace %} to $1.50 at the {% place "dakota-hotel-mandan" %}Dakota{% endplace %} and {% place "merchants-hotel" %}Merchants{% endplace %} hotels. The InterOcean and Nigey hotels charged $2.25 and up. The {% place "city-cafe-hotel-nigey" %}City Cafe{% endplace %} served hotel guests and downtown workers. {% person "l-s-schaff" %}L. S. Schaff{% endperson %} operated the restaurant from 1939 through 1941. In January 1941, its space was remodeled with a horseshoe-shaped counter and reopened as {% place "steins-eat-shop" %}Stein's Eat Shop{% endplace %} under {% person "eddie-stein" %}Eddie Stein{% endperson %}.</p>

